{"node":{"id":"MONDO:0007600","label":"primary Fanconi syndrome","definition":"A condition in which the kidneys do not absorb certain substances into the body. These substances, such as cysteine, fructose, galactose, or glycogen, are lost in the urine. Fanconi syndrome is thought to be caused by genetic and environmental factors, and it may be diagnosed at any age. Symptoms of Fanconi syndrome include increased urine production (which may cause dehydration), weakness, and abnormalities of the bones.","synonyms":["FRTS1","Fanconi renotubular syndrome 1","primary Fanconi renotubular syndrome"],"xrefs":["GARD:0009118","MEDGEN:341765","NCIT:C123229","Orphanet:3337","UMLS:C1857395"],"parents":[],"parents_labels":{},"children":["MONDO:0024525"],"children_labels":{"MONDO:0024525":"Fanconi renotubular syndrome 1"},"in_core":false,"cluster_id":7,"is_group":false,"n_genes":4,"n_phenotypes":29,"mechanism_classes":[]},"genes":[{"id":"e_cf194bde2065","source":"MONDO:0007600","target":"EHHADH","type":"caused_by","evidence":[{"db":"Orphanet","origin":"Orphanet","record":"ORPHA:3337","level":"curated","date":"2026-06-23","url":"https://www.orpha.net/en/disease/detail/3337","confidence":0.95,"snippet":"Disease-causing germline mutation(s) in (Assessed) — enoyl-CoA hydratase and 3-hydroxyacyl CoA dehydrogenase"},{"db":"HPO","origin":"Orphanet","record":"ORPHA:3337","level":"curated","date":"2026-09-02","confidence":0.9,"url":"https://hpo.jax.org/browse/disease/ORPHA:3337","snippet":"EHHADH is annotated as disease gene of ORPHA:3337 (HPO genes_to_phenotype, Orphanet-derived)"}],"contradicting":[],"confidence":0.95,"independent_sources":["Orphanet"],"level":"curated"},{"id":"e_b66e1e3bdd08","source":"MONDO:0007600","target":"GATM","type":"caused_by","evidence":[{"db":"Orphanet","origin":"Orphanet","record":"ORPHA:3337","level":"curated","date":"2026-06-23","url":"https://www.orpha.net/en/disease/detail/3337","confidence":0.95,"snippet":"Disease-causing germline mutation(s) in (Assessed